<Placemark><name>1. Start – Jung-dong Station</name><description><![CDATA[Line 2, one stop past Haeundae. Walk down to the east end of Haeundae Beach and start climbing Dalmaji-gil.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13479674?lng=129.1683320&lat=35.1666790&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>129.168332,35.166679,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Mipo – Blueline Park</name><description><![CDATA[Foot of the hill. The Blueline Park beach train and sky capsule run from here along the coast if you want to skip the climb back.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1007574852?lng=129.1728560&lat=35.1581380&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>129.172856,35.158138,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Dalmaji-gil cherry road</name><description><![CDATA[The classic stretch: cherry trees over the winding road with the sea below, galleries and cafés at the top. The Moontan Road forest trail runs parallel just above.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13491814?lng=129.1842300&lat=35.1607520&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>129.184230,35.160752,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Cheongsapo</name><description><![CDATA[Small fishing harbour with the red-and-white lighthouses; grilled clams and the Daritdol skywalk.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13491720?lng=129.1924120&lat=35.1604130&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>129.192412,35.160413,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. End – Songjeong Station</name><description><![CDATA[Donghae Line back towards Centum City and Bujeon. Songjeong Beach is 10 min from the station if you still have legs.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/325631241?lng=129.2020720&lat=35.1877050&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>129.202072,35.187705,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Nakdong embankment, Samnak (2.4 km)</name>
<Placemark><name>Gwaebeop-Renecite Stn → Nakdong embankment cherry road → Samnak Ecological Park, 2.4 km</name><description><![CDATA[2.4 km<br>1. Levee and riverside path (pedestrian router; the cherry tunnel is on top of the embankment) (approx.)]]></description><styleUrl>#line-3</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>128.977229,35.163123,0 128.976989,35.163157,0 128.976792,35.163183,0 128.976712,35.163195,0 128.976056,35.163294,0 128.975905,35.163317,0 128.975507,35.161965,0 128.975402,35.162122,0 128.975419,35.162265,0 128.975521,35.162676,0 128.975693,35.163360,0 128.975808,35.163959,0 128.975831,35.164166,0 128.975845,35.164716,0 128.975931,35.165124,0 128.975995,35.165568,0 128.975999,35.165593,0 128.975999,35.165593,0 128.976200,35.166880,0 128.976281,35.167657,0 128.976325,35.167928,0 128.976334,35.167985,0 128.976255,35.168425,0 128.976202,35.168534,0 128.975781,35.168565,0 128.975246,35.168673,0 128.975260,35.169273,0 128.975282,35.170267,0 128.975307,35.171448,0 128.975262,35.172024,0 128.975262,35.172024,0 128.975156,35.173374,0 128.974937,35.175640,0 128.974811,35.176613,0 128.974783,35.177058,0 128.974745,35.177989,0 128.974631,35.178761,0 128.974539,35.179676,0 128.974543,35.179991,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>1. Start – Gwaebeop-Renecite Station exit 1</name><description><![CDATA[Gimhae light rail, direct from Gimhae Airport (15 min) or one stop from Sasang (line 2). Exit 1 faces the river park.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/21404544?lng=128.9772960&lat=35.1634400&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>128.977296,35.163440,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Nakdong embankment cherry road</name><description><![CDATA[Long, flat tunnel of cherry trees on top of the levee, with the Nakdong River and Samnak Park below. Walk north; it is quietest early morning.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1959451958?lng=128.9759870&lat=35.1655940&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1582-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>128.975987,35.165594,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. End – Samnak Ecological Park</name><description><![CDATA[Drop down into the park for wetlands, bike rental and canola fields in April. Return the same way or continue north along the river.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/31927837?lng=128.9736610&lat=35.1690450&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>128.973661,35.169045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
